[{:db/id "q-105748/selection/05a86ea952710d7414329341d6fa14faffb71e1c67ae490e5724c79b41d2461c" :answer/id #uuid "5f7b0f52-436d-5620-8460-1342248586c4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-64x+32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105748/selection/01dc8923b564b9810c4a42470d2a402d5e779b70d4b258c625e58ab237e02a04" :answer/id #uuid "50f75880-5423-5413-91cf-8905c8b404ea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}+64x+32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105748/selection/5707d075bf5de2dda48cd4fc79b95a112b678f15fd9437c5b276da61518076a9" :answer/id #uuid "f40449d6-6900-5f7f-8606-4009e8670601" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+8{x}^{3}-36{x}^{2}-64x+16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105748/selection/a8dac12c0d615aa4d0668bb1235b9bc785ca6b121dbed01dbf1c45bcbd877ef5" :answer/id #uuid "e5b15e4e-f853-5223-920e-547d6175fb2e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105748/selection/eb87cb537337dd3f3f6d3bbda413c0e15305cf115133f7240319f597c4d0f525" :answer/id #uuid "c75a1e97-739a-5760-b690-f6e54434ef3a" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2{x}^{4}+10{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}+64x+16" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-105748/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "344bf595-272b-5b00-933f-9c597371a388" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-105748/selection/a8dac12c0d615aa4d0668bb1235b9bc785ca6b121dbed01dbf1c45bcbd877ef5" :answer-field/choices ["q-105748/selection/05a86ea952710d7414329341d6fa14faffb71e1c67ae490e5724c79b41d2461c" "q-105748/selection/01dc8923b564b9810c4a42470d2a402d5e779b70d4b258c625e58ab237e02a04" "q-105748/selection/5707d075bf5de2dda48cd4fc79b95a112b678f15fd9437c5b276da61518076a9" "q-105748/selection/a8dac12c0d615aa4d0668bb1235b9bc785ca6b121dbed01dbf1c45bcbd877ef5" "q-105748/selection/eb87cb537337dd3f3f6d3bbda413c0e15305cf115133f7240319f597c4d0f525"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-105748" :question/id #uuid "278ce71d-00cf-5c20-9289-38eadcd1be8f" :question/math-academy-id "q-105748" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}={x}_{4}=2,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =2(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x-2)(x-2)(x-2)(x-2) & =2({x}^{2}-4x+4)({x}^{2}-4x+4) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+4{x}^{2}-4{x}^{3}+16{x}^{2}-16x+4{x}^{2}-16x+16) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-8{x}^{3}+24{x}^{2}-32x+16) \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{4}-16{x}^{3}+48{x}^{2}-64x+32.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-105748/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-105748"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-107795/selection/422ad605102220b3aa8054932e9219744faa2b849ed86b9d95ad34c617caf718" :answer/id #uuid "b26e71eb-8845-5d6b-8c9a-4b6b60874a28" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}+5{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+12x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107795/selection/1afccf91da216f71ca77632e852e60d3512beb22e4e3f197e84caf815ee1e47b" :answer/id #uuid "78cab7f7-1ae2-5578-8c97-a1e8664e49a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107795/selection/a3433e9dd6f83d398f12d6fca20e2ed916d41cf5a9c398da9c900ba71326fe4d" :answer/id #uuid "d255d045-ef7c-59ed-8133-f6358d42c9eb" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}-4{x}^{3}+6x-32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107795/selection/11b82e671753e131291b7a723dcca64c086ac766f86aa6bffefa0dc8c43b0ba2" :answer/id #uuid "a9422069-f2b7-5e56-8646-56eae72b341f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-13{x}^{2}+24x-32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107795/selection/5baad1dc513440ef9eaea536873ead13803131b04cb59960d72deec6702bc1d9" :answer/id #uuid "642df560-da71-590c-a8d2-4ee7a0b90265" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "{x}^{4}-5{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}+8x-32" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-107795/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "c2023096-467d-5dde-b600-395eae870341" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-107795/selection/1afccf91da216f71ca77632e852e60d3512beb22e4e3f197e84caf815ee1e47b" :answer-field/choices ["q-107795/selection/422ad605102220b3aa8054932e9219744faa2b849ed86b9d95ad34c617caf718" "q-107795/selection/1afccf91da216f71ca77632e852e60d3512beb22e4e3f197e84caf815ee1e47b" "q-107795/selection/a3433e9dd6f83d398f12d6fca20e2ed916d41cf5a9c398da9c900ba71326fe4d" "q-107795/selection/11b82e671753e131291b7a723dcca64c086ac766f86aa6bffefa0dc8c43b0ba2" "q-107795/selection/5baad1dc513440ef9eaea536873ead13803131b04cb59960d72deec6702bc1d9"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-107795" :question/id #uuid "66a0bb88-71dc-5b62-903b-60d272d88560" :question/math-academy-id "q-107795" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=1,{x}_{2}=2,{x}_{3}=-4$ and ${x}_{4}=4$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Find $P(x).$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}=1,{x}_{2}=2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-1)(x-2)(x-(-4))(x-4) \\\\  & =(x-1)(x-2)(x+4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-1)(x-2)(x+4)(x-4) & =({x}^{2}-3x+2)({x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-16{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3}+48x+2{x}^{2}-32 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-14{x}^{2}+48x-32.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-107795/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-107795"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319949/field-1/c9fbc3e00c873490a4e05c6dcaaf5975e025547dbed010137cc2494ad5afa265" :answer/id #uuid "8e4928f5-aff4-569f-99c7-91a38ac66f00" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "9x^4+36x^3-108x^2-576x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319949/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "6fb52441-f7d4-5050-a525-a1939bb526d3" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319949/field-1/c9fbc3e00c873490a4e05c6dcaaf5975e025547dbed010137cc2494ad5afa265" :answer-field/choices ["q-319949/field-1/c9fbc3e00c873490a4e05c6dcaaf5975e025547dbed010137cc2494ad5afa265"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319949" :question/id #uuid "d28d5124-469a-5f65-a3be-7cbfc59abf13" :question/math-academy-id "q-319949" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $9.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,576$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}=-2,$ ${x}_{3}=-4,$ and ${x}_{4}=4,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=9,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =9(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-(-4))(x-4) \\\\  & =9(x+2)(x+2)(x+4)(x-4)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}9(x+2)(x+2)(x+4)(x-4) & =9({x}^{2}+4x+4)({x}^{2}-16) \\\\  & =9({x}^{4}-16{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-64x+4{x}^{2}-64) \\\\  & =9({x}^{4}+4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-64x-64) \\\\  & =9{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-108{x}^{2}-576x-576.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=9{x}^{4}+36{x}^{3}-108{x}^{2}-576x-576.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319949/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319949"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319369/field-1/1accd9ce2250b493468c84a72762152c8344424ff640f396bc6b598bed9678f6" :answer/id #uuid "231a6c66-6af6-5e0a-a5a3-f3e49b84564f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^4+x^3-18x^2-52x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319369/field-1/0c1fa05bb59b9e7328ab4dd885805acb87683633e94ab1f3bb7bec7137ec3daa" :answer/id #uuid "158c8e1e-fd39-57da-a0e6-1f7666a5b978" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^4+x^3-18x^2+52x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319369/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "8add5f23-ddad-5b5a-b410-78fbba64bbe8" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319369/field-1/1accd9ce2250b493468c84a72762152c8344424ff640f396bc6b598bed9678f6" :answer-field/choices ["q-319369/field-1/1accd9ce2250b493468c84a72762152c8344424ff640f396bc6b598bed9678f6" "q-319369/field-1/0c1fa05bb59b9e7328ab4dd885805acb87683633e94ab1f3bb7bec7137ec3daa"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319369" :question/id #uuid "d5cee7fe-1c83-5fa8-92d1-eceb09bbcaf5" :question/math-academy-id "q-319369" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and ${x}_{4}=5$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,40$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-2,$ and ${x}_{4}=5,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =1(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-(-2))(x-5) \\\\  & =(x+2)(x+2)(x+2)(x-5)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+2)(x+2)(x+2)(x-5) & =({x}^{2}+4x+4)({x}^{2}-3x-10) \\\\  & ={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-10{x}^{2}+4{x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}-40x+4{x}^{2}-12x-40 \\\\  & ={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}-52x-40.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)={x}^{4}+{x}^{3}-18{x}^{2}-52x-40.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319369/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319369"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-319377/field-1/7b81a3a83c0028067153c3fdfad59c6441779ba652c3db1845690d469bf764f1" :answer/id #uuid "18d4dfac-ca77-5d5e-aa0b-879bd902e88f" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "2x^4-12x^2-16x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-319377/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "1fd529b3-9c60-5e22-8225-34f7d41c3a99" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-319377/field-1/7b81a3a83c0028067153c3fdfad59c6441779ba652c3db1845690d469bf764f1" :answer-field/choices ["q-319377/field-1/7b81a3a83c0028067153c3fdfad59c6441779ba652c3db1845690d469bf764f1"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-319377" :question/id #uuid "e9516825-da50-5582-90ed-716cd564fd9c" :question/math-academy-id "q-319377" :question/problem "The quartic polynomial $P(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-1,$ and ${x}_{4}=3$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $2.$ Determine the **expanded form** of $P(x).$\n\n$P(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,6$" :question/worked-solution "Since our quartic polynomial has roots ${x}_{1}={x}_{2}={x}_{3}=-1,$ and ${x}_{4}=3,$ and the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=2,$ we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) & =2(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-(-1))(x-3) \\\\  & =2(x+1)(x+1)(x+1)(x-3)\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2(x+1)(x+1)(x+1)(x-3) & =2({x}^{2}+2x+1)({x}^{2}-2x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}-3{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3}-4{x}^{2}-6x+{x}^{2}-2x-3) \\\\  & =2({x}^{4}-0{x}^{3}-6{x}^{2}-8x-3) \\\\  & =2{x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-16x-6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $P(x)=2{x}^{4}-12{x}^{2}-16x-6.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-319377/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "7a64d73a-2983-5d05-9aa0-4582b2e7aee1"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-319377"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-8210"] :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/07724ed5ffd4843ab0a23b0029eeec6291ae698aba71f56f99fb7ac565287932.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Find $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-1,$ ${x}_{2}=4,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 2\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-(-1))(x-4)(x-(-2\\text{i}))(x-(2\\text{i})) \\\\  & =1(x+1)(x-4)(x+2\\text{i})(x-2\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x+1)(x-4)(x+2\\text{i})(x-2\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+x-4x-4)({x}^{2}+(2\\text{i}-2\\text{i})x-(2\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-3x-4)({x}^{2}+4) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+4{x}^{2}-3{x}^{3}-12x-4{x}^{2}-16 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}-3{x}^{3}-12x-16.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-320074/field-1/ec40e94ef5631ec0054767aacf080d6b940229ce94819ff2201ac52826dbf659" :answer/id #uuid "24a51abe-b716-5c14-b918-1bd85f0bcaa4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^4+21x^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320074/field-1/d604c071eb5969f1b79dff2bf91a73185e30e99c28ca664c217430dad66dc5de" :answer/id #uuid "b61e801d-c689-5e03-a1f7-ea427a430255" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "x^4-21x^2" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320074/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "669d6088-8a14-5435-8756-3e848a70ff16" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320074/field-1/ec40e94ef5631ec0054767aacf080d6b940229ce94819ff2201ac52826dbf659" :answer-field/choices ["q-320074/field-1/ec40e94ef5631ec0054767aacf080d6b940229ce94819ff2201ac52826dbf659" "q-320074/field-1/d604c071eb5969f1b79dff2bf91a73185e30e99c28ca664c217430dad66dc5de"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320074" :question/id #uuid "021b26bc-0ff0-575c-a6e8-6605470c927a" :question/math-academy-id "q-320074" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/fb8d76e5fb2e83676fbab4178b523bf8cbff076490f12fa8be17c37ce06e1820.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $1.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,100$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 5\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=1.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =1(x-2)(x-(-2))(x-5\\text{i})(x-(-5\\text{i})) \\\\  & =(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}(x-2)(x+2)(x-5\\text{i})(x+5\\text{i}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}+2x-2x-4)({x}^{2}+5\\text{i}x-5\\text{i}x-(5\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ ({x}^{2}-4)({x}^{2}+25) & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+25{x}^{2}-4{x}^{2}-100 & = \\\\ {x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)={x}^{4}+21{x}^{2}-100.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320074/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320074"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-320292/field-1/3ee78a5503cf59e6c91e0bb8b9d890038cd4e81f10162cc63c04ac4435a34802" :answer/id #uuid "070f6cda-b78c-5c39-865d-d6cec8d18555" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x^4-6x^3+18x^2-24x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-320292/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "46d227b6-12ef-52ca-951f-3033e6d3d9a7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-320292/field-1/3ee78a5503cf59e6c91e0bb8b9d890038cd4e81f10162cc63c04ac4435a34802" :answer-field/choices ["q-320292/field-1/3ee78a5503cf59e6c91e0bb8b9d890038cd4e81f10162cc63c04ac4435a34802"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-320292" :question/id #uuid "201097fd-4f47-5897-ac43-904b3aaad274" :question/math-academy-id "q-320292" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/4eafeae1c77e3e75cb2b281181346eeb7e96ca5e1bd15ec11d722109469557a1.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$+\\,24$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1,2}=\\pm 2\\text{i}$  and ${x}_{3,4}=1\\pm \\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x-(-2\\text{i}))(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) \\\\  & =3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i}))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x-2\\text{i})(x+2\\text{i})(x-(1+\\text{i}))(x-(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+2\\text{i}x-2\\text{i}x-(2\\text{i})^{2})({x}^{2}-x(1-\\text{i})-x(1+\\text{i})+(1+\\text{i})(1-\\text{i})) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+4)({x}^{2}-2x+2) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+2{x}^{2}+4{x}^{2}-8x+8) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}-2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}-8x+8) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}-6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}-24x+24\\,.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-320292/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-320292"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-275317/field-1/ce73dfb107ee8900360834bd44740dbd3cd46b1d57406b4fa27f3f0f196b0a4a" :answer/id #uuid "08c2cd94-45b2-5f67-acad-7ee02acd2f6e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x^4+6x^3+18x^2+54x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275317/field-1/604bbcfaf093f7fa2c3674af6c3a45fe1e21a89fab0b0c1bbd57cac3f1f62a74" :answer/id #uuid "1f17c198-f797-5db0-b6c5-784e2f9431f5" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "3x^4+6x^3+18x^2-54x" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-275317/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "581a2041-b571-5130-b013-20e48f898225" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-275317/field-1/ce73dfb107ee8900360834bd44740dbd3cd46b1d57406b4fa27f3f0f196b0a4a" :answer-field/choices ["q-275317/field-1/ce73dfb107ee8900360834bd44740dbd3cd46b1d57406b4fa27f3f0f196b0a4a" "q-275317/field-1/604bbcfaf093f7fa2c3674af6c3a45fe1e21a89fab0b0c1bbd57cac3f1f62a74"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-275317" :question/id #uuid "76ebd207-119e-52cd-b4d5-03e4755976db" :question/math-academy-id "q-275317" :question/problem "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14066605/assets/431ba020bfc39615e1d49a866c6ee7c30cf8cc8f84ebde6866ef0e0cb9c8708b.png)\n\nThe Argand diagram above shows the roots of a quartic polynomial $f(x).$ Determine the **expanded form** of $f(x)$ given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $3.$\n\n$f(x)=$\n{{field-1}}\n$-\\,81$" :question/worked-solution "From the diagram, we see that $f(x)$ has roots ${x}_{1}=-3,$ ${x}_{1}=1,$ and ${x}_{3,4}=\\pm 3\\text{i}.$ Additionally, we're given that the coefficient of the quartic term is $a=3.$ Therefore, we can write the polynomial as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}f(x) & =a(x-{x}_{1})(x-{x}_{2})(x-{x}_{3})(x-{x}_{4}) \\\\  & =3(x-(-3))(x-1)(x-(-3\\text{i}))(x-3\\text{i}) \\\\  & =3(x+3)(x-1)(x+3\\text{i})(x-3\\text{i})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nExpanding the parentheses, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3(x+3)(x-1)(x+3\\text{i})(x-3\\text{i}) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}-x+3x-3)({x}^{2}-3\\text{i}x+3\\text{i}x-(3\\text{i})^{2}) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{2}+2x-3)({x}^{2}+9) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+9{x}^{2}+2{x}^{3}+18x-3{x}^{2}-27) & = \\\\ 3({x}^{4}+2{x}^{3}+6{x}^{2}+18x-27) & = \\\\ 3{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}+54x-81 & .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $f(x)=3{x}^{4}+6{x}^{3}+18{x}^{2}+54x\\,-81.$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-275317/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "5eda5034-e8a8-5260-8dc0-6c663880fe9e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-275317"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-8212/selection/2feb62ffca4a39a3811176f3a82edc2ff66df7cedfe67e8cec762eb12f0cefc2" :answer/id #uuid "159a62f5-39ca-5f8d-974d-981cfa7554b4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value